# PANOSETI gRPC Environment Configuration (.env_example)
#
# These variables are read by DaqDataGatewayServicer.startup() (only relevant
# when running `pseti-grpc server --profile gateway` or `--profile headnode`,
# i.e. `daq_data.role = "gateway"` in the server config) as a fallback for
# the [daq_data.gateway] daq_config_path / network_config_path fields in
# server_gateway.toml / server_headnode.toml. Precedence: the TOML config
# value always wins when set; these env vars are only consulted when the
# corresponding TOML field is left empty.
#
# This lets a fleet-wide value be provided once (e.g. via docker-compose's
# --env-file, a systemd unit's EnvironmentFile=, or exported in the shell
# before running `pseti-grpc server`) instead of hand-editing
# server_gateway.toml/server_headnode.toml on every node.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and uncomment the values you need, then wire it
# into however you launch the server (this repo has no built-in .env loader
# of its own -- unlike panoseti's `pseti` CLI).

# ==============================================================================
# DaqData Gateway Configuration
# ==============================================================================

# Path to the daq_config.json that lists all edge DAQ nodes the gateway
# should fan in. Only consulted when [daq_data.gateway] daq_config_path is
# left empty ("") in server_gateway.toml / server_headnode.toml.
# No default -- if neither is set, the gateway logs a warning and starts
# with zero edge nodes contacted.
# PSETI_GRPC_DATA_CONFIG=/path/to/panoseti-software/control/configs/daq_config.json

# Path to network_config.json for port-forwarding overrides (optional --
# only needed when an edge node is reached through a forwarded gateway IP
# rather than directly). Only consulted when
# [daq_data.gateway] network_config_path is left empty ("") in
# server_gateway.toml / server_headnode.toml.
# No default -- if neither is set, the gateway proceeds without any
# port-forwarding overrides (a warning is logged, but this is not fatal).
# PSETI_GRPC_NETWORK_CONFIG=/path/to/panoseti-software/control/configs/network_config.json
